            "content": "Treatment with complement inhibitors, such as the C5 inhibitors eculizumab and ravulizumab, is the standard of care for patients with PNH and has been proven to dramatically reduce the risk of thrombosis. By blocking the cleavage of complement protein C5, these drugs prevent the formation of C5a and the C5b-9 membrane attack complex. This halts intravascular hemolysis and mitigates the downstream effects that drive thrombophilia, such as platelet activation and endothelial dysfunction. Clinical studies and long-term data have shown that treatment with C5 inhibitors reduces the rate of thromboembolic events in PNH patients by approximately 85-90% compared to untreated patients, transforming the natural history of the disease and significantly improving survival."
